{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Nandiya","html":"<article id='thag1.25'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.25 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.25 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Tatiyavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Three </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Nandiyattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Nandiya </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Obhāsajātaṁ phalagaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Dark One, after attacking such a monk—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>cittaṁ yassa abhiṇhaso; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>one who has arrived at the fruit, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tādisaṁ bhikkhumāsajja, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and whose mind is always full of light—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>kaṇha dukkhaṁ nigacchasī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>you’ll fall into suffering. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Nandiyo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
